; fas9_table_layout.scr - step 9.5 (table layout, *T block, proxy graphics, extents), F9.5. Run it with
;   python -I tools/fas9_facit_run.py doc/facit/fas9_table_layout.scr --input doc/facit/acad_2018_dxf_tables.dxf
; on AutoCAD 2025's core (plain commands, no LISP). The input is the table Erik made in AutoCAD's GUI with
; doc/facit/12_tables.scr (text in all three row types, a formula, merged cells with a fill, borders of other weights,
; a field, a block cell with auto-fit, a cell with two contents); the core has no cell editor (TABLEDIT picks a cell and
; ends, no -TABLESTYLE), so the layout branches the GUI file does not show are made by the commands the core has, each
; one change from the input (the drawing is taken back with U after each):
;
;   moved, rotated 30 degrees and 90 degrees   the proxy graphics' transform and the table's horizontal direction (11)
;   mirrored                                    what AutoCAD does to a table (the cells' text is not mirrored)
;   scaled 2 and 0.5                            the table's sizes and text heights, margins and the *T block
;   color, lineweight, layer of the table       what ByBlock and ByLayer are in the *T block and its proxy graphics
;   a text style with another font              the table's text laid out in another font (a regeneration recomputes
;                                               the table)
;
; What it cannot make is "ej testat" in doc/plans/2026-10-27-fas-9-typer.md (Utfall 9.5) and doc/facit/fas9_notes/F9.5.md:
; text rotation and fonts of single cells, an edited merge, borders and fills of a cell, the blocks' auto-fit after a
; cell change, a table style of other margins or row types (the core has no cell editor and no table style command).
;
; The table is picked by a window around it (the field's line and the MTEXT of 12_tables.scr are outside it).
;EXPECT ACAD_TABLE
;SAVE table_layout
_.UNDO
_M
_.MOVE
_W
-1,5
141,81

0,0
25,-10
;SAVE table_layout moved
_.UNDO
_B
_.ROTATE
_W
-1,5
141,81

0,80
30
;SAVE table_layout rotated30
_.UNDO
_B
_.ROTATE
_W
-1,5
141,81

0,80
90
;SAVE table_layout rotated90
_.UNDO
_B
_.MIRROR
_W
-1,5
141,81

0,0
100,0
_N
;SAVE table_layout mirrored
_.UNDO
_B
_.MIRROR
_W
-1,5
141,81

0,0
0,100
_N
;SAVE table_layout mirrored_vertical
_.UNDO
_B
